    <statement><p>Find the equation of the ellipse with the given properties:</p>
<p>Foci <m>(0, \pm 5)</m> and two vertices at <m>(\pm 2,0)</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/><m>=1</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{x^{2}}{4}+\frac{y^{2}}{29}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>{\left(\frac{x}{a}\right)}^{2}+{\left(\frac{y}{b}\right)}^{2}=1</m>. 

 The foci are
<m>\left(0, \pm c\right)</m> on the
<m>y</m>-axis with
<m>c=5</m>,  and two vertices are at
<m>\left(\pm  a, 0\right)</m> with
<m>a=2</m>.

 We use the relation
<m>c=\sqrt{{b}^{2}-{a}^{2}}</m> to find
<m>b</m>:
<me>b=\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{c}^{2}}=\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{5}^{2}} = \sqrt{29}</me>
Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is
<me>{\left(\frac{x}{2}\right)}^{2}+{\left(\frac{y}{\sqrt{29}}\right)}^{2}=1.</me> 


</solution>
